{
  "document": "[page 1]\n           Analytic Verification AV-11 - Rev B\n\n1. Objective\nVerify the released nominal magnetic circuit against closed-form analytic calculations under the linear\nquasi-static assumptions.\n\n2. Test configuration\n\n Parameter                                     Value\n a                                                 0.025 m\n  l                                                 0.150 m\n delta                                            0.00150 m nominal\n mu_r                                         1200\n sigma                                              0.08\n N_exc / N_meas                               600 / 50 turns\n Frequency                                    50 Hz\n Current ramp                                  0 A before 0.10 s; linear to 2.0 A RMS at 0.50 s; hold through 1.0 s\n\n3. Analytic checks at 2 A RMS\n\n Quantity                                          Expected\n Total core reluctance                                  5.289249e+05 A/Wb\n Air-gap reluctance                                    1.909859e+06 A/Wb\n Equivalent gap/leak reluctance                          1.757071e+06 A/Wb\n Total core flux                                         5.249354e-04 Wb\n Useful air-gap flux                                      4.829406e-04 Wb\n Leakage flux                                           4.199483e-05 Wb\n Core B                                               0.839897 T\n Gap B                                               0.772705 T\n Core magnetic drop                                    277.651 A-turn\n Gap magnetic drop                                     922.349 A-turn\n Exciting induced |U|                                     98.948 V RMS\n Measuring induced |U|                                   7.586 V RMS\n\n4. Acceptance\nMMF balance residual shall be within 0.5% of N*I. Useful/core flux ratio shall be 0.92 within 0.002 absolute.\nFlux, B, H and induced-voltage magnitudes shall each agree within 1% of the released analytic result.\n[page 1 also supplied as visual image 1]",
